    <string name="gpu_err">The kernel refused the module</string>
    <string name="gpu_about">When large free blocks run out, the Adreno driver makes the kernel free memory on the spot, and the thread drawing the frame waits. This loads a small kernel module that tells the driver to take smaller blocks instead.</string>
    <string name="gpu_cost">GPU memory is built from smaller blocks more often.</string>
