    <string name="reserve_na">Not available on this kernel</string>
    <string name="reserve_about">Android keeps a small reserve of free memory. When apps use it up faster than it is refilled, they wait while memory is freed. This starts freeing at about 3 percent of RAM free instead of under 1 percent.</string>
    <string name="reserve_cost">That memory is not used for cache or background apps.</string>
