    <string name="keep_total">%1$s of %2$s kept</string>
    <string name="keep_count">%1$d of %2$d switched on</string>
    <string name="keep_about">Under memory pressure Android drops or compresses parts of these processes, and a frame waits while they are read back. Each one you switch on lives in a memory group that is never swapped, and what it works with is never reclaimed.</string>
    <string name="keep_cost">That memory is not available to other apps.</string>
    <string name="keep_na_official">This Android already keeps them in RAM itself</string>
